---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro-expressive-code/components';
import {
  HOMEPAGE_EXAMPLE_NMBL, HOMEPAGE_EXAMPLE_HTML,
  FEATURE_EMBEDDED_MD,
  COMMENT_VISIBILITY, COMMENT_VISIBILITY_HTML,
  COMMENT_ATTR, COMMENT_ATTR_HTML,
} from '../examples';
---

<BaseLayout title="Home">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1><span class="hero-mark">&gt;&lt;</span> NMBL</h1>
      <p class="acronym"><strong>N</strong>o <strong>M</strong>ore <strong>B</strong>rackets <strong>L</strong>anguage</p>
      <p class="tagline">A shorthand notation for HTML<br/>built for modern web frameworks and token efficiency.</p>
      <p class="tagline-sub">Closing tags, angle brackets, id/class attributes &mdash; NMBL strips the noise so you and your AI can <b>do more with less</b>.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a href="/playground" class="btn btn-primary">Try the Playground</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="benefits">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="benefits-grid">
        <div class="benefit">
          <h3>Easier to read</h3>
          <p>Indentation shows structure. No extra unnecesary closing tags or brackets to scan past. You see the content and hierarchy immediately.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="benefit">
          <h3>Faster to write</h3>
          <p>CSS selector shorthand for ids and classes. Implicit <code>div</code> tags. No need to reformat to keep indentiation clean. A typical template is 30&ndash;40% shorter than equivalent HTML.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="benefit">
          <h3>Increased token efficiency</h3>
          <p>Every <code>&lt;/div&gt;</code> and <code>class=</code> burns tokens unnecesarily. NMBL allows LLMs to save their context window by removing boilerplate.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="benefit">
          <h3>Fits your stack</h3>
          <p>Use <code>&lt;template lang="nmbl"&gt;</code> in Vue SFCs. Drop in the Vite plugin. Add the Astro integration. NMBL compiles to standard HTML &mdash; any framework already understands.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="benefit">
          <h3>(Almost) Nothing to learn</h3>
          <p>NBML is not a new language - it's a shorthand that maps directly to HTML. Give it 10 minutes and it will click.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="comparison">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Same structure. Less noise.</h2>
      <div class="comparison-grid">
        <div class="comparison-pane">
          <div class="comparison-label">NMBL &mdash; {HOMEPAGE_EXAMPLE_NMBL.split('\n').length} lines, {HOMEPAGE_EXAMPLE_NMBL.length} chars</div>
          <Code code={HOMEPAGE_EXAMPLE_NMBL} lang="nmbl" frame="none" />
        </div>
        <div class="comparison-pane">
          <div class="comparison-label">HTML &mdash; {HOMEPAGE_EXAMPLE_HTML.split('\n').length} lines, {HOMEPAGE_EXAMPLE_HTML.length} chars</div>
          <Code code={HOMEPAGE_EXAMPLE_HTML} lang="html" frame="none" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="comments-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Comments that actually work.</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle">HTML has no way to comment out an attribute. Most template languages inherit that limitation. NMBL treats comments as a first-class feature &mdash; with control over what reaches production.</p>

      <div class="comments-grid">
        <div class="comment-card">
          <h3>You control what ships</h3>
          <p>Use <code>//</code> for developer notes that are <strong>stripped from output</strong> &mdash; TODOs, debug notes, nothing ships to production. Use <code>//!</code> when you <strong>explicitly want</strong> an HTML comment in the output.</p>
          <div class="comment-compare">
            <div class="comment-pane">
              <div class="comment-pane-label">NMBL</div>
              <Code code={COMMENT_VISIBILITY} lang="nmbl" frame="none" />
            </div>
            <div class="comment-pane">
              <div class="comment-pane-label">HTML output</div>
              <Code code={COMMENT_VISIBILITY_HTML} lang="html" frame="none" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="comment-card">
          <h3>Comments inside attributes</h3>
          <p>Something HTML and every other template language lack: comment out individual attributes while debugging. Use <code>//</code> for single-line or <code>/* */</code> for inline &mdash; toggle attributes without deleting them.</p>
          <div class="comment-compare">
            <div class="comment-pane">
              <div class="comment-pane-label">NMBL</div>
              <Code code={COMMENT_ATTR} lang="nmbl" frame="none" />
            </div>
            <div class="comment-pane">
              <div class="comment-pane-label">HTML output</div>
              <Code code={COMMENT_ATTR_HTML} lang="html" frame="none" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="features">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Features</h2>
      <div class="features-grid">
        <div class="feature">
          <h3>CSS-like selectors</h3>
          <p>Use <code>#id</code> and <code>.class</code> shorthand directly on elements. Implicit <code>div</code> when using selectors alone.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <h3>Block expansion</h3>
          <p>Nest single children inline with <code>&gt;</code> syntax. Perfect for navigation lists: <code>li &gt; a(href="/") Home</code></p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <h3>Embedded languages</h3>
          <p>Use content modes to embed markdown, CSS, or any language inline. Attach a filter to transform the content at compile time &mdash; <code>div:md</code> to embed markdown, <code>script:</code> for raw script blocks, or register your own.</p>
          <div class="feature-code">
            <Code code={FEATURE_EMBEDDED_MD} lang="nmbl" frame="none" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <h3>Bidirectional</h3>
          <p>Convert HTML to NMBL and back. The decompiler produces clean, idiomatic NMBL from any HTML input. Drop in existing HTML and start editing in NMBL immediately.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: 6rem 0 4rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    font-size: 4rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .hero-mark {
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
  }

  .acronym {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .acronym strong {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .tagline {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto 0.75rem;
  }

  .tagline-sub {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: white;
  }

  .btn-primary:hover {
    background: var(--color-accent-hover);
    color: white;
  }

  .benefits {
    padding: 3rem 0 4rem;
  }

  .benefits-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .benefit {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .benefit h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .benefit p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .benefit code {
    background: rgba(124, 110, 246, 0.15);
    padding: 0.125rem 0.375rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .comparison {
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }

  .comparison h2 {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .comparison-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--color-border);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .comparison-pane {
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .comparison-label {
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    background: var(--color-bg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .comparison-pane :global(.expressive-code) {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .comparison-pane :global(.expressive-code figure) {
    margin: 0;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 0;
  }

  .comparison-pane :global(.expressive-code pre) {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 0;
  }

  .comments-section {
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }

  .comments-section h2 {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .section-subtitle {
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto 2rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .comments-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .comment-card {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .comment-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .comment-card p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .comment-card code {
    background: rgba(124, 110, 246, 0.15);
    padding: 0.125rem 0.375rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .comment-compare {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--color-border);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .comment-pane {
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .comment-pane-label {
    padding: 0.375rem 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    background: var(--color-bg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .comment-pane :global(.expressive-code) {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .comment-pane :global(.expressive-code figure) {
    margin: 0;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 0;
  }

  .comment-pane :global(.expressive-code pre) {
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 0;
  }

  .features {
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }

  .features h2 {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .features-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .feature {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .feature h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .feature p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .feature code {
    background: rgba(124, 110, 246, 0.15);
    padding: 0.125rem 0.375rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .feature-code {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .feature-code :global(.expressive-code) {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .feature-code :global(.expressive-code figure) {
    margin: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 6px;
  }

  .feature-code :global(.expressive-code pre) {
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .hero h1 {
      font-size: 2.5rem;
    }

    .benefits-grid,
    .comparison-grid,
    .features-grid,
    .comments-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .comment-compare {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
